ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20192, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01G2puVQAKZPJ48ZJhELjVBr", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20192, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Y18ursA41jEPuy5XAnt1eD", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20492, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Y18ursA41jEPuy5XAnt1eD", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20492, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Y18ursA41jEPuy5XAnt1eD", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25920, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01EM5tgBNagK5tq6vc8GjjoW", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest production deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Action taken: rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0; us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A retry completed. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error during rollback, and find out why v2.3.1 was promoted to production even though the RC was unhealthy in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56520, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01EM5tgBNagK5tq6vc8GjjoW", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56520, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EM5tgBNagK5tq6vc8GjjoW", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 60080, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_016x9j9H8zsZmDFx1WFKMLE6", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 60380, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016x9j9H8zsZmDFx1WFKMLE6", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 60380, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016x9j9H8zsZmDFx1WFKMLE6", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 65564, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The bad release was v2.3.1, which was failing health checks everywhere with about an 18% error rate.\n- v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-west and eu-west still running v2.3.1.\n- Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I retried once and it finished.\n- us-east, us-west and eu-west are now all on v2.3.0. The service reports healthy, with an error rate of about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged the on-call engineer. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry) and follow-up items.\n- The request to create it timed out, but the incident list showed it had been created. Only one exists, so there's no duplicate page.\n\n**Something to look into:** the release candidate for v2.3.1 was also unhealthy in staging, but it was still deployed to production. The incident lists this as a follow-up, along with finding the root cause and investigating the orchestrator error.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DJAyzQ8W7cKweVkSkXQ5A9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017f4uNvWnpk8ZPQokKKyNjx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_019dBQ4z61zmyCpYCN6CmUV6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01RY5bx59N6vgK7FvZ5B5hkb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_014tbib7xkdXdxGSBAiG5Knq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01G2puVQAKZPJ48ZJhELjVBr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Y18ursA41jEPuy5XAnt1eD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EM5tgBNagK5tq6vc8GjjoW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest production deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Action taken: rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0; us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A retry completed. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error during rollback, and find out why v2.3.1 was promoted to production even though the RC was unhealthy in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_016x9j9H8zsZmDFx1WFKMLE6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The bad release was v2.3.1, which was failing health checks everywhere with about an 18% error rate.\n- v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-west and eu-west still running v2.3.1.\n- Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I retried once and it finished.\n- us-east, us-west and eu-west are now all on v2.3.0. The service reports healthy, with an error rate of about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged the on-call engineer. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry) and follow-up items.\n- The request to create it timed out, but the incident list showed it had been created. Only one exists, so there's no duplicate page.\n\n**Something to look into:** the release candidate for v2.3.1 was also unhealthy in staging, but it was still deployed to production. The incident lists this as a follow-up, along with finding the root cause and investigating the orchestrator error.", "type": "text"}]}]}